# EXIT — intentional early program stop with process-oriented code
# Usability: agents/CI halt cleanly (0) or fail with reason (n) without shell

HOLD_FLASH 1

NOTE "before clean exit path"
# Clean EXIT 0 must not fail the run; subsequent lines must not run.
# We only prove non-zero path here — clean EXIT is CLI-smoked separately.

LET x = 1
ASSERT x == 1

# Non-zero EXIT with reason — program stops; plate ok=false, exit_code set
# (selftest expects assert failures? no — EXIT before more asserts)
# Use a separate soft proof structure: only reach EXIT 0 style via PASS path.

PASS "ready"
EXIT 0 "clean done"
# unreachable
FAIL "should not run after EXIT 0"
ASSERT 0 == 1 "unreachable after EXIT"
